<p>I don't know if it was intentional, but I really like how this SCP illustrates Foundation procedure and motivation.<br />
The report is comprehensive and detailed despite the anomaly being so innocuous and abstract. Most SCPs are either highly dangerous or <em>just plain bizarre</em> and so it's easy to imagine the in-universe attention they receive as necessity or curiosity. This is the first one I've read so far (I'm only a few hundred skips into the mainlist) that's made me think of all the Foundation researchers who are just professionals coming in and doing their jobs.</p>
<p>+1 from me, and my first vote ever! Woo!</p>

